@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: end to end, per harness on kit v3: where a credential lives, who declares it, which one the agent uses, and what proveo observes
' covers: internal/sbx/secret.go
' covers: internal/sbx/bindings.go, internal/sbx/bindings_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/credential_report.go, internal/backend/sandbox/credential_report_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/opencode_engine.go (createOpenCodeEngine stdin)
' covers: internal/sbx/secret_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/run.go (AuthLoginArgs)
' covers: internal/sbx/upstream.go (UpstreamKitFor, keepHooks)
' covers: internal/sbx/third_party/*.yaml (credential@1, lifecycle@1)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (Spec secrets loop, agentCredentials, backAPIKeys, storedAPIKeys)
' covers: internal/credentials/hints.go (StoreHolds, NoCredentialHint)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/workload_test.go
' covers: internal/credentials/storename.go (StoreName)
' covers: internal/credentials/login.go (NeedsSandboxLogin), internal/credentials/login_test.go
' covers: internal/secretref/secretref.go (SbxSource), internal/secretref/secretref_test.go
' covers: e2e/secret_source_test.go
' covers: internal/run/run.go (StoredAPIKeys wiring, reportSandboxLogin)
' covers: internal/run/params.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_credentials.go (provisionSlot)
' covers: e2e/ladder_test.go
'   which auth var a run chooses ..... _spec/internal/credentials/credential-decisions.puml
'   what proveo can read on the host .. _spec/internal/secretref/secret-references.puml
'   local edits to upstream kits ...... _spec/internal/sbx/vendored-kit-deltas.puml
'   the credential boundary ........... _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml
'
' ── DECISION 2026-10-28 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The Executor chose "One end-to-end credential spec": consolidate
' credential-path, oauth-provisioning, kit-sandbox-credential-gap and
' backed-api-key-env into one decision table before any code change.
' Constraints, verbatim: "support only kit v3", "Keep credentials as `sbx`
' native as possible". This spec replaces those four. Their mixin-era and
' docker-broker history is dropped; their kit-v3 rules are below as R1–R8.
'
' ── THE SIX LAYERS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   L1 host source      shell env, the project .env, op:// refs (secretref), the darwin Keychain
'   L2 registry         internal/provider: env var → service, hosts, header
'   L3 sbx store        HOST-WIDE, outlives every run; one entry per name; a
'                       service entry holds an API key ("(stored)") or an OAuth
'                       login ("(oauth configured)"), never both visibly
'   L4 declaration      credential@1 in the workload: the upstream kit's (copied
'                       by UpstreamKitFor) plus proveo's (agentCredentials)
'   L5 sandbox render   what sbx materialises: SBX_CRED_<SVC>_MODE, placeholder
'                       env vars (apiKey.proxyManaged), OAuth credential files
'                       holding sentinels; the proxy swaps sentinels at egress
'   L6 agent state      the credential the agent actually sends: its own config
'                       or store, which can hold a login the agent made itself
'
' ── DECISION TABLE (kit v3; MEASURED unless marked) ─────────────────────────
' harness    │ L3 entries read           │ L4 declared by                         │ L5 render                                     │ L6 agent uses                              │ proveo observes
' ───────────┼───────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────
' claudecode │ anthropic (key | OAuth)   │ upstream claude: anthropic, apiKey     │ ~/.claude/.credentials.json (sk-ant-oat01-    │ .credentials.json; key outranks OAuth      │ L3 names (sbx secret ls),
'            │                           │ ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OAuth file          │ proxy-managed); settings.json from MODE       │ upstream                                   │ NeedsSandboxLogin pre-launch
' codex      │ openai (key | OAuth)      │ upstream codex: openai, apiKey         │ install hook writes ~/.codex/config.toml by   │ codex; forced_login_method="api" blocks    │ L3 names only
'            │                           │ OPENAI_API_KEY, OAuth sentinels        │ SBX_CRED_OPENAI_MODE (oauth: sandboxd provider│ an in-sandbox login in managed modes       │
'            │                           │                                        │ with the oai-oat01 sentinel bearer)           │                                            │
' cursor     │ cursor (key | OAuth)      │ upstream cursor: cursor, apiKey        │ CURSOR_API_KEY=<placeholder> only when backed │ env key; else cursor's own login, which    │ L3 names (APIKeyServices)
'            │                           │ CURSOR_API_KEY; proveo backAPIKeys     │ (backAPIKeys); OAuth via in-sandbox sign-in   │ sbx captures at /auth/poll                 │
'            │                           │ sets proxyManaged when stored          │                                               │                                            │
' opencode   │ anthropic, github, google,│ upstream opencode: 7 services; proveo  │ placeholder env per proxyManaged key; openai  │ opencode v2 SQLite via `opencode auth      │ L3 names; the credentials
'            │ groq, openai(+OAuth),     │ agentCredentials for stored services   │ OAuth → ~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json;    │ import` (upstream hook, jq); a login made  │ line names the RUN's auth
'            │ openrouter, xai, opencode,│ upstream lacks (opencode, moonshot, …) │ the hook imports it as sbx-openai             │ inside opencode persists and stays active  │ var, not L6
'            │ moonshot, …               │                                        │                                               │                                            │
' hermes     │ the services proveo       │ proveo only (no upstream kit):         │ placeholder env per declared key              │ hermes config  [Unverified]                │ L3 names only
'            │ declares                  │ agentCredentials                       │                                               │                                            │
'
' ── RULES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' R1 sbx is the only broker. On the default `--credentials broker`, no value
'    rides argv, the workload, or the agent env; proveo writes it to the store
'    host-side with the value on stdin. `--credentials forward` passes a bare
'    `-e NAME`, and the posture line reads "forward (the key rides the sandbox env)".
' R2 ONE ROUTE, SERVICE IDS ONLY (P2, 2026-10-28). Every API key goes to
'    `sbx secret set <service>` under its registry id (StoreName; six ids break
'    the _API_KEY pattern), and the workload declares credential@1 for that
'    service when upstream does not (agentCredentials: stored, or stored by
'    this run). P0 M1 measured that any service id injects once bound, so the
'    experimental `set-custom` route (customSecretTarget, SecretSetCustom*,
'    BuiltinServices) is deleted. `proveo init` writes the service id and
'    nothing else; StoreHolds and NoCredentialHint read and name services.
'    `proveo init` lists every entry sbx never reads — an env-var or def name,
'    a `-sub` name, a custom secret on a registry provider's variable — with the
'    `sbx secret rm` that removes it (StaleStoreEntries); it removes nothing.
' R3 A declared, stored, bound service writes the header itself. MEASURED
'    2026-10-27 (N14), sbx 0.50.0, GET opencode.ai/zen/v1/models: no header
'    sent → the proxy wrote Authorization from the `opencode` entry (401 on a
'    bad key). A custom secret only substitutes its own sbx-cs-… placeholder.
' R4 OAuth slots have sbx as their only writer. A plan token
'    (CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN) is never stored (P2): StoreName returns its
'    service with kind StoreSubscription, the run prints the sbx sign-in
'    (sbx.SignIn), and `proveo init` shows a locked sign-in row per harness. anthropic: an in-sandbox
'    sign-in sbx captures (`sbx run claude <ws> -- auth login`, AuthLoginArgs).
'    openai: `sbx secret set openai --oauth` on the host (MEASURED 2026-10-28,
'    Fedora: "openai (oauth configured)"), or an in-sandbox sign-in. proveo never
'    imports a host OAuth blob; the darwin Keychain blob has no destination.
' R5 An API key outranks OAuth on the same service (upstream). So a run never
'    stores an API key on a service with an OAuth slot (sbx.OAuthServices:
'    anthropic, openai) and says so. MEASURED 2026-09-24: a forwarded key had
'    landed in the anthropic entry, the listing still read "(oauth
'    configured)", and SBX_CRED_ANTHROPIC_MODE=apikey billed later sandboxes.
' R6 Upstream declares its services; proveo declares only the rest. The
'    workload copies every upstream credential@1 and lifecycle hook verbatim
'    (keepHooks drops two named exceptions). agentCredentials adds a service
'    only when upstream lacks it AND the store holds it, since an unbacked
'    declaration makes sbx ask a human. backAPIKeys sets apiKey.proxyManaged
'    for apiKeyEnvWhenBacked = {cursor} when stored: upstream withholds it
'    because cursor reads a set-but-unbacked CURSOR_API_KEY as invalid
'    (sbx-kits-contrib cursor/README; sbx-releases#259).
' R7 The GLOBAL store is host-wide and persistent: a global write
'    authenticates every later sandbox. Since P3 only `proveo init` writes
'    globally; a run writes into its own sandbox's scope (R12). sbx validates no
'    name: `sbx secret set <anything>` stores a TYPE "service" entry.
' R8 A subscription harness with no credential anywhere (NeedsSandboxLogin: no
'    file login, nothing stored for its services, no provider key — a plan
'    token in the env no longer counts, R4) gets the sbx sign-in printed, never
'    run: the sign-in needs a browser and a person. P3 deleted the darwin
'    Keychain reader (ReadKeychainLogin, KeychainLogin, PROVEO_KEYCHAIN_SERVICE):
'    a host OAuth blob has no destination, so reading it only produced advice.
'
' R9 APPROVALS GATE THE API KEY, NOT THE OAUTH LOGIN. MEASURED 2026-10-28,
'    sbx 0.50.0, `sbx create` without a terminal:
'      proveo-probe-m1 key, no binding → "WARN: credential not sent: no binding
'        authorizes this service", no header (M1); with an apiKey binding → injected.
'      groq key (a BUILT-IN service), no binding → same WARN, SBX_CRED_GROQ_MODE=none (M6).
'      openai OAuth login, binding with apiKey ONLY → "✓ OpenAI — using stored
'        OAuth credentials", SBX_CRED_OPENAI_MODE=oauth (M7, codex's credential@1
'        copied verbatim). The bindings file's `oauth` block is not consulted.
'    On a terminal, `sbx create` asks ("This kit wants to use these credentials …
'    1. Approve all 2. Review each 3. No"); declining left credentials.yaml
'    unchanged. proveo now gives `sbx create` the terminal (consentInteractive:
'    a TTY stdin and no PROVEO_SCHEDULE), so sbx's own prompt is reachable.
'    Before create, reportCredentials prints one line per declared service the
'    store holds something for — sbx.Mechanism: an approved key, else a stored
'    OAuth login, else "withheld" — and refuses an UNATTENDED create whose own
'    service (chosenService: the auth var's provider, else the built-in agent's
'    subscription service) has only an unapproved key, printing the
'    credentials.yaml block that approves it. proveo never writes that file.
' R11 REFERENCES ARE sbx SOURCES (P3, F3). A provider variable may hold a
'    reference instead of a value. proveo never resolves it: ProviderLookup hands
'    it back as written, and secretref.SbxSource maps it to sbx's own flags —
'      keychain:<item>  → --command '/usr/bin/security find-generic-password -w -s <item>'
'      pass:<entry>     → --command 'pass show <entry> | head -n 1'
'      cmd:<command>    → --command '<command>'
'      op://… | arn:aws:secretsmanager:… → --ref <it>
'      env:<VAR>        → the value of VAR on stdin
'    The item name is single-quoted, so it cannot break out of the command.
'    `--credentials forward` (or a provider sbx cannot inject) refuses a
'    reference, because the variable would ride the agent env. `proveo init`
'    registers an imported or typed reference globally the same way.
'    MEASURED: M3 (global --command, live refresh), M8 (sandbox-scoped
'    --command set before create). Linux `pass` not measured.
' R12 A RUN WRITES ONLY INTO ITS OWN SANDBOX (P3, F2). Spec's secrets loop runs
'    `sbx secret set --force <service> --sandbox <name> [source]`: scoped
'    entries outrank global ones, apply live, and leave with `sbx rm` (P0 M5).
'    The P1 report reads the global rows plus this sandbox's
'    (sbx.StoreEntriesFor). TestAReferenceReachesTheSandboxAsAScopedSbxSource
'    (e2e) stores a cmd: reference this way and reads the injected header.
' R10 After the session, while the sandbox still runs, reportCredentialInUse
'    reads the agent's own credential state through `sbx exec` (read-only) and
'    names whether sbx manages it: opencode `auth export` (active `sbx-*` record
'    or an agent-owned login that outranks sbx), codex ~/.codex/auth.json and
'    claude ~/.claude/.credentials.json (sentinel or not). A stopped sandbox is
'    skipped, because `sbx exec` restarts it. MEASURED live on this Mac
'    (`proveo run codex`, OAuth): "codex uses sbx's credential (sentinel in its
'    credential file)".
'
' ── WHAT WENT WRONG, MEASURED 2026-10-28 (opencode + ChatGPT, Fedora) ──────
' L3 lacked the OAuth login → fixed by R4's host command.
' L6 held an in-agent `chatgpt-token-sharing` login (a real token, active),
'    which upstream's hook leaves alone by design.
' L5→L6 import failed on a jq compile error, and the hook exits 0 on every
'    failure → vendored-kit-deltas.puml DELTA 1.
' proveo printed "opencode: using OPENCODE_API_KEY" throughout. The posture
' reports the run's chosen auth var (credential-decisions.puml), and nothing
' compares it with L6.
'
' ── OBSERVATION GAP (the reason for this table) ─────────────────────────────
' proveo observes L1–L3 and its own L4. It never reads L5 or L6 after start.
' Each failure above was silent at the layer where it happened. Closing that
' gap the sbx-native way means reading what sbx already exposes — `sbx exec`
' for SBX_CRED_*_MODE and the agent's own export (`opencode auth export`,
' `~/.codex/auth.json` mode, `.credentials.json` sentinel) — rather than
' proveo holding or rewriting credentials. Undecided; the table comes first.
'
' ── P0 MEASUREMENTS, 2026-10-28 (macOS, sbx 0.50.0) ────────────────────────
' Probe workloads FROM proveo/codex:local, credential@1 injecting Bearer on
' httpbin.org/headers (which echoes the request), throwaway service ids and
' values; credentials.yaml backed up and restored byte-identical.
' M1 an arbitrary service id (`proveo-probe-m1`) injects once a binding
'    approves it: "Authorization: Bearer <stored value>". Unbound: `sbx create`
'    prints "WARN: credential not sent: no binding authorizes this service",
'    injects nothing, and STILL sets the env var to "proxy-managed".
'    SBX_CRED_<SVC>_MODE exists only for sbx's built-in services.
' M2 an env-var-named entry is never read: store holding only GROQ_API_KEY,
'    workload declaring service groq (bound) → SBX_CRED_GROQ_MODE=none, no
'    header; adding `groq` → mode apikey, header injected.
' M3 `sbx secret set <svc> --command '/usr/bin/security find-generic-password
'    … -w' --refresh on-demand`: the host resolves it, the header carries the
'    Keychain value, and a changed Keychain value reaches the RUNNING sandbox on
'    the next request. Linux (`pass show`) not measured.
' M4 the global anthropic OAuth login reaches a fresh sandbox through the claude
'    kit's own credential@1: ~/.claude/.credentials.json holds the sentinels,
'    and GET api.anthropic.com/api/oauth/profile (OAuth-only) answers 200 with
'    the account. The in-sandbox `/login` itself needs a person; not driven.
' M5 `sbx secret set <svc> --sandbox <name>` works BEFORE the sandbox exists,
'    overrides the global entry in a running sandbox, `sbx secret rm <svc>
'    --sandbox <name>` falls back to the global value live, and `sbx rm` of
'    the sandbox deletes its scoped entries.
'
' ── OPEN ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' O1 RESOLVED by M2 and P2: env-var-named entries are dead, proveo no longer
'    writes them, and `proveo init` lists the old ones with their `sbx secret rm`.
'    Before P2: `proveo init` writes each
'    key under the service AND every env-var name (provisionSlot), so this
'    Mac's ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, CURSOR_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY,
'    OPENCODE_API_KEY and XAI_API_KEY entries inject nothing [Inference: by M2's
'    mechanism, not probed one by one] and outlive every run (R7).
' O2 RESOLVED by P2 (R4): the plan token is no longer stored. Before P2:
'    CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN mapped through StoreName to a subscription name
'    ("claudecode"), not a service. No workload declares `claudecode`, so by
'    M1/M2 the entry is unread [Inference]. M4 shows the global OAuth slot is
'    what a claude sandbox uses.
' O5 M4 injected OAuth while SBX_CRED_ANTHROPIC_MODE read `none`; Fedora's
'    opencode run read SBX_CRED_OPENAI_MODE=oauth. Kit hooks gate on these
'    variables (claude's "Seed Claude settings.json from SBX_CRED_ANTHROPIC_MODE"),
'    so a `none` that is wrong mis-seeds them. Cause unmeasured.
' O6 M1: an UNBOUND proxyManaged key still exports its sentinel, so an agent
'    that treats a set variable as a chosen key (cursor) sees a dead one
'    whenever the binding is missing, not only when the store is.
' O3 RESOLVED for opencode by P4 (vendored-kit-deltas.puml DELTA 2): sbx's record
'    is activated over an agent-owned login. Before P4:
'    Only codex's kit blocks an in-sandbox login in managed modes
'    (forced_login_method = "api"). opencode's and cursor's kits do not, so an
'    agent-owned login can override sbx's credential (MEASURED for opencode).
' O4 hermes has no upstream kit. docker/sbx-kits-contrib#423 (open) proposes
'    Docker-managed Codex OAuth for hermes; adopting it would move hermes to R6.
title Credential resolution on kit v3 — six layers, one winner per agent

rectangle "L1 host source\nenv · .env · op:// · Keychain" as L1 <<host>>
rectangle "L2 registry\ninternal/provider" as L2 <<app>>
database "L3 sbx store\nHOST-WIDE · service ids" as L3 <<db>>
rectangle "L4 credential@1\nupstream kit + agentCredentials" as L4 <<app>>
rectangle "L5 sandbox render\nMODE · placeholders · files" as L5 <<cloud>>
rectangle "L6 agent state\nthe credential it sends" as L6 <<cloud>>

L1 ARROW_MAIN L2 : env var → service
L2 ARROW_MAIN L3 : sbx secret set <service> (stdin)
L3 ARROW_MAIN L4 : binding by service
L4 ARROW_MAIN L5 : sbx renders at create/start
L5 ARROW_MAIN L6 : agent config / import hooks
L6 ARROW_ERROR L1 : proveo never reads L5/L6

note right of L3
  **One store for the whole host.**
  A write from any run authenticates
  every later sandbox (R7); an API key
  outranks OAuth on a service (R5).
end note

note right of L4
  **Upstream declares, proveo fills.**
  Every upstream credential@1 and hook
  is copied; proveo adds only stored
  services upstream lacks (R6).
end note

note right of L6
  **The agent picks the winner.**
  A login it made itself persists and
  can stay active over sbx's sentinel
  (O3); nothing reports which won.
end note
@enduml
